    "# Notebook 03: MentalBERT Classification Demo\n",
    "## Digital Mental Health NLP Pipeline for Asian Adolescents — Tier 1 Screening\n",
    "\n",
    "**Author:** Lin Fang Yu 林芳伃 | MPH Candidate, NUS  \n",
    "**Date:** May 2026  \n",
    "\n",
    "### Objectives\n",
    "This notebook demonstrates **Tier 1 Screening** — the first stage of the pipeline that classifies text as distress / no distress using **Chinese MentalBERT**.\n",
    "\n",
    "We cover:\n",
    "1. Loading and preparing the preprocessed dataset\n",
    "2. Setting up Chinese MentalBERT for classification\n",
    "3. Running inference on sample texts\n",
    "4. Evaluating classification performance\n",
    "5. Visualising model confidence and attention patterns\n",
    "6. Analysing misclassifications with clinical interpretation\n",
    "\n",
    "### Why MentalBERT?\n",
    "\n",
    "| Model | F1 on Chinese MH Data | Notes |\n",
    "|---|---|---|\n",
    "| **Chinese MentalBERT** | **88.39%** | Domain-specific pre-training on MH social media |\n",
    "| Chinese BERT (general) | ~72% | No mental health domain adaptation |\n",
    "| Multilingual BERT | ~68% | English-dominant; poor on non-Latin scripts |\n",
    "| GPT-4 (zero-shot) | ~74% | Misses indirect Asian distress expression |\n",
    "\n",
    "> **Ethics Note:** This notebook uses synthetic/publicly available data only. No real patient data. Clinical deployment requires IRB approval and institutional governance.\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n"
   ]
  },
